{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4698",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa5 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which then participates in the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase, ultimately leading to Ndufa5 being a participant in this process. This indicates a potential mechanism where Metformin influences the function of Nadh Dehydrogenase, which in turn affects Ndufa5. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, reinforcing the notion that Metformin may modulate the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase, thereby influencing Ndufa5. The overlapping pathways and the shared role of Nadh Dehydrogenase in the interaction highlight a possible mechanism by which Metformin could impact Ndufa5, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
